_audit_update_record             
;
2023-05-01 deposited with the CCDC.	2026-11-05 downloaded from the CCDC.
;
_vrf_PLAT234_ac672new            
;
PROBLEM: Large Hirshfeld Difference O12      --C58   .    0.45 Ang.  
RESPONSE: This error may arise due to the unequal magnitude of components of
the anisotropic displacement parameters along chemical bonds or a
disorderred structure or sometimes due to over-refinement. However the data parameter
are well conveged with excellent GOOF.
;
_vrf_PLAT375_ac672new            
;
PROBLEM: Strange C-O-H Geometry (C-O  >   1.45 Ang) .....  O11 Check
RESPONSE: Thermal disorder in the dangling chiral moiety also this is a
data recorded with Mo X-ray source. 
;
_vrf_PLAT312_ac672new            
;
PROBLEM: Strange C-O-H Geometry (C-O  >   1.25 Ang) .....  O12 Check
RESPONSE: See response above. 
;
_vrf_PLAT417_ac672new            
;
PROBLEM: Short Inter D-H..H-D   H7A  ..H11  .   1.38 Ang.  
RESPONSE: It is difficult to locate hydrogen atoms accurately using X-ray data
partcularly when heavy metal atoms are present. Therefore methods are adopted 
to add hydrogen atoms in coordinated or lattice water molecules, including 
DIF-Fourier maps and DFIX/DANG instructions. H4A & H4B are added using riding 
model whereas H14 are fixed using AFIX13 command. 
;
